KPUL0 1.1.0
# A hand-written fixture, NOT generated. Its job is to FAIL to load, exercising the
# MIN_CONSUMER gate (R4) specifically.
#
# The container version is DELIBERATELY one this reader supports. An earlier draft said
# KPUL0 9.0.0, and review caught that the reader rejects that at the container-major check
# BEFORE it ever reads MIN_CONSUMER -- so the fixture passed with UnsupportedVersion even if
# the min_consumer gate were broken. A test that passes for the wrong reason guards nothing.
#
# needs_a_newer_container.l0 covers the container check separately.
MIN_CONSUMER 9.0.0
OPSET tile 1.0.0
PRODUCER hand-written 1.0.0
PROGRAM "needs a newer reader"
VALUES none
OPERAND "A" rows=16 cols=16 tile_rows=16 tile_cols=16
OP kind=FEED in=A:0,0 port_kind=input port="West"
END
